# Frontend design schema

Canonical tokens live in `apps/web/src/index.css` under `:root`. Treat that file as the **single source of truth** for surfaces, typography, radius, and default shadows.

## Tokens (reference)

| Token | Role |
|-------|------|
| `--bg`, `--fg`, `--fg-muted` | Page background, primary text, secondary text (~60% feel—use muted for hints) |
| `--accent`, `--accent-hover`, `--accent-fg`, `--focus-ring` | Primary actions, focus ring, emphasis borders |
| `--card`, `--card-border`, `--control-shadow`, `--shadow` | Elevated surfaces and separation |
| `--positive-*`, `--negative-*` | Market movement, status badges, and error states |
| `--radius`, `--radius-sm` | Default and smaller corner radius |
| `--font` | Inter stack; body already sets `font-family` — inherit in components |

## Rules

1. **Prefer CSS variables** for layout chrome: backgrounds, borders, foreground, accents. Avoid new hard-coded hex/rgb except for **meaning-specific** hues (e.g. market up/down) until those become named tokens in `:root`.
2. **Add new primitives in `:root` first**, then wire components with `var(--…)`—do not scatter one-off palette values across TSX or CSS without a matching token when the color is reused.
3. **Focus**: use `:focus-visible` patterns consistent with globals (accent outline)—do not remove focus outlines without an accessible replacement.
4. **Consistency**: spacing and component layout follow existing patterns in `app.css`; match established gaps (e.g. `rem`-based grids) unless changing the shell intentionally.

### Example

```css
/* Good */
.panel {
  background: var(--card);
  border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  color: var(--fg);
}

/* Avoid when a semantic token fits */
.panel {
  background: #ffffff;
  color: #2b302b;
}
```

When introducing dark mode later, extend the schema with a class or `prefers-color-scheme` block on the same token names rather than branching colors inside every component.
